{{!-- One subject and how it stands: an image beside a title, an optional value
      opposite it, and an optional bar beneath.

      Distinct from `identity`, which is the chip -- avatar, name, sub-line, one
      line tall. A subject is the block: the image spans both lines, so the title
      and the bar sit beside it rather than under it. With no bar it collapses to
      one line and the image shrinks to match, which is the common case of a small
      picture beside a title.

      The bar is rendered by the meter or gauge part through the same renderer,
      not reimplemented here, so it cannot drift from the standalone one. That is
      the only nesting in the system and it is deliberate -- see the plan.

      A subject can be the click target itself rather than carrying a button. It
      stays a div and gains role and tabindex: the delegated dispatcher binds
      Enter and Space for anything that is not already a button, so a clickable
      part is reachable from the keyboard without wrapping a meter in a <button>. --}}
<div class="cpb-part-subject{{#unless bar}} cpb-subject-compact{{/unless}}{{#if action}} cpb-subject-clickable{{/if}}"
     {{#if action}}role="button" tabindex="0"
     data-cpb-module="{{moduleId}}" data-cpb-action="{{action}}"
     {{#if actionValue}}data-cpb-value="{{actionValue}}"{{/if}}
     {{#if tooltip}}data-tooltip="{{tooltip}}"{{/if}}{{/if}}>

    {{#if img}}
    <img class="cpb-part-subject-img{{#if framed}} cpb-subject-img-framed{{/if}}" src="{{img}}" alt="" />
    {{/if}}

    <div class="cpb-part-subject-body">
        <div class="cpb-part-subject-head">
            {{#if index}}<span class="cpb-part-subject-marker cpb-subject-number">{{index}}</span>{{/if}}
            {{#if icon}}<i class="cpb-part-subject-marker {{icon}}"></i>{{/if}}
            <span class="cpb-part-subject-title">{{{title}}}</span>
            {{#if value}}<span class="cpb-part-subject-value">{{{value}}}</span>{{/if}}
        </div>
        {{#if bar}}{{{bar}}}{{/if}}
    </div>
</div>
